","The staging of oral cavity cancer involves the evaluation of various factors, including physical examination, imaging, and biopsy. Radiographic findings alone are insufficient to diagnose extranodal extension (ENE) in the oral cavity cancer staging. While imaging techniques such as CT scans, MRI scans, and PET scans can help identify areas of tumor spread, they may not provide enough information to confirm if the tumor extends outside the lymph nodes.

