In the case of parasites, the overuse of antibiotics can also lead to the development of resistance through horizontal gene transfer, where resistant genes are passed from one parasite to another, even if they are of different species. This can happen through the transfer of plasmids or other mobile DNA structures.

The overuse of antibiotics in parasitic infections can have serious consequences, as it can lead to treatment failures, increased healthcare costs, and increased risk of complications and infections. Additionally, it can contribute to the development of multi-resistant strains that are difficult to treat with any available antibiotics.

