   \text{Equivalents} = \text{Normality} \times \text{Volume (in liters)} = 2.00 \, \text{N} \times 10.0 \, \text{L} = 20.0 \, \text{eq}
   \]
   Since H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) is diprotic, 1 mole provides 2 equivalents. Thus, the equivalents are equivalent to:
   \[
   20.0 \, \text{eq} = 10.0 \, \text{mol}
   \]

2. **Calculate the total equivalents of H\(_2\)SO\(_4\) required in the final solution:**
   \[
   \text{Equivalents} = \text{Molarity} \times \text{Volume (in liters)} = 3.00 \, \text{M} \times 20.0 \, \text{L} = 60.0 \, \text{mol}
   \]
