**Relationship between vapor pressure and PEL:**  
The vapor pressure of a liquid is a measure of its tendency to change into a gas. A higher vapor pressure means the liquid is more likely to evaporate and form a vapor. The PEL (Permissible Exposure Limit) is the maximum concentration of a substance in a gas mixture that a person can tolerate without experiencing harmful effects.  

