2. Solubility in water: Magnesium chloride is highly soluble in water, which is a common property of ionic compounds. The polar water molecules can surround and separate the charged ions, allowing the compound to dissolve.

3. Electrical conductivity: Magnesium chloride is an good conductor of electricity when dissolved in water or in the molten state. This is because the ions are free to move and carry an electric charge.

