","To determine which sulfides precipitate when \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) is added to the given mixture, we compare the solubility product (\( K_{sp} \)) of the sulfides formed by each ion. The sulfides with \( K_{sp} \) values less than the ion product (\( K_{sp} = [\text{M}^{2+}][\text{S}^{2-}] \)) will precipitate.

1. **\( \text{Mn}^{2+} \):** The sulfide of manganese is \( \text{MnS} \). Its \( K_{sp} \) is approximately \( 10^{-19} \).
2. **\( \text{Ni}^{2+} \):** The sulfide of nickel is \( \text{NiS} \). Its \( K_{sp} \) is approximately \( 10^{-21} \).
3. **\( \text{Cu}^{2+} \):** The sulfide of copper is \( \text{CuS} \). Its \( K_{sp} \) is approximately \( 10^{-30} \).
4. **\( \text{Hg}^{2+} \):** The sulfide of mercury is \( \text{HgS} \). Its \( K_{sp} \) is approximately \( 10^{-54} \).

