Since there is a difference in electronegativity between carbon and oxygen, the bond between them is polar. However, CO2 has a linear molecular geometry with the oxygen atoms on opposite sides of the carbon atom. This symmetry causes the bond dipoles to cancel each other out, resulting in a nonpolar CO2 molecule overall.
