\[
\text{pH} = -\log (10^{-4}) = 4
\]  
A solution with pH < 7 is acidic, a solution with pH = 7 is neutral, and a solution with pH > 7 is basic. Since pH = 4, the solution is \(\boxed{\text{acidic}}\).

