Given $f(n)=1+ \frac {1}{2}+ \frac {1}{3}…+ \frac {1}{n} (n\in\mathbb{N}^{*})$, it is calculated that $f(2)= \frac {3}{2}$, $f(4) > 2$, $f(8) > \frac {5}{2}$, $f(16) > 3$, $f(32) > \frac {7}{2}$. Conjecture the expression for $f(2^{n}) >$ ______ when $n\geqslant 2$.<end_of_turn>
