   \]
   \[
   v_{\text{Earth}} \approx -6.7 \times 10^{-24} \text{ m/s}
   \]

The negative sign indicates that the Earth's velocity is directed opposite to the direction of the cannonball's motion. The magnitude of the recoil velocity is extremely small, as the Earth's large mass damresses the effect of the cannonball's momentum. Thus, the Earth's recoil is negligible for practical purposes.
