","The unitarity condition for the \(S\)-matrix is derived from the conservation of probability in quantum mechanics. The \(S\)-matrix describes the amplitude for a system to transition from state \(m\) to state \(n\) after an interaction. The probability of this transition is given by \(|\delta_{mn}|^2 = |\delta_{mn}|^2\). The unitarity condition ensures that the probability is conserved, i.e., the sum of probabilities of all possible transitions from state \(m\) is 1. 

