\[
\mathcal{V}_2 = -\frac{d}{dt} \left( N_2 \frac{N_1 I_1(t) A}{\ell} \right) = -\frac{N_2 N_1 A}{\ell} \frac{d I_1(t)}{dt}
\]
The r.m.s. voltage of the source is related to the current by:
\[
V_0 = \sqrt{\frac{1}{T} \int_0^T I_1^2(t) \, dt}
