   \[
   0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{r^{1.4-1}} \implies r^{0.4} = \frac{1}{1 - 0.56} = \frac{1}{0.44} \implies r = (2.727)^{2.5} \approx 3.5
   \]

2. **Work Done (\( w \))**:
   The work done per kg of air is related to the heat rejected (\( Q_r \)) and the cycle efficiency:
   \[
   w = \eta Q_r = 0.56 \times 544 \, \text{kJ/kg} = 300.24 \, \text{kJ/kg}
   \]

