2. Let the final momentum of the system be \(P_{\text{final}} = m_{\text{cannonball}} v_{\text{cannonball}} + m_{\text{Earth}} v_{\text{Earth}}\), where \(m_{\text{cannonball}} = 1 \text{ kg}\), \(v_{\text{cannonball}} = 90.0 \text{ m/s}\), \(m_{\text{Earth}} = 5.97 \times 10^{24} \text{ kg}\), and \(v_{\text{Earth}}\) is the recoil velocity of the Earth.

3. By momentum conservation, \(P_{\text{initial}} = P_{\text{final}}\), so:
   \[
